        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yves Apollinaire Pede, Nelson Mandela\n- Places: Abomey, South Africa\n- Organizations: Abomey Museum\n- Roles: Vodou artist, President of South Africa\n- Topics: sand paintings, anti-apartheid\n\nFacts:\n- Nelson Mandela was born on 18 July 1918 and died on 5 December 2013.\n- Nelson Mandela was a South African anti-apartheid revolutionary, politician, and philanthropist.\n- Nelson Mandela served as President of South Africa from 1994 to 1999.\n- Yves Apollinaire Pede was born in 1959 in Abomey.\n- Yves Apollinaire Pede is a Beninois Vodou artist.\n- After Yves Apollinaire Pede was commissioned to reproduce reliefs for the Abomey Museum, he made sand paintings of well-known personalities such as Nelson Mandela.",
